From that lineage this project inherits the single response envelope, the typed
boundary-refusal vocabulary, the restart-safe job store and detached background
worker, the wall-clock budget model, and the workspace-root resolution rules.

The agy runtime adapter -- discovery, argument construction, stream parsing,
outcome classification and the read-only workspace mirror -- was written against
behaviour measured directly from the Antigravity CLI and is documented in
docs/AGY-RUNTIME-CONTRACT.md. The mirror design and the measured contract come
from the sibling project agy-plugin-cc
(https://github.com/handong66/agy-plugin-cc), Apache-2.0.

